    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπ-εύς</span></b> , gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆος</span>, ὁ, 
			Att.
		pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					85
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπός</span>):—<i>one who
				attends</i> or <i>escorts, conductor, guide,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.325
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				376
			</span></i>; of favourable winds, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖροι νηῶν πομπῆες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.362
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who takes part in a procession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.334.14
			</span></i>.</div>
